Krita Nova 76 - Transform bar: the mode menu switches the mode (Android)

The transform bar's mode menu (patch 72) ran its own event loop from the
press (QMenu::exec); on Android the tap on a mode could get lost - the
mode stayed Free Transform - and the bar or the tool could go away while
the menu was open, which could crash Krita. The menu now opens without
an event loop of its own (popup; deleted when closed), the chosen mode is
set once the menu has closed, and it is set through
KisToolTransform::novaSetTransformMode, which also works when the tool
options widget has not been made.

diff --git a/plugins/tools/tool_transform2/kis_tool_transform.cc b/plugins/tools/tool_transform2/kis_tool_transform.cc
index 3267946..f06af84 100644
--- a/plugins/tools/tool_transform2/kis_tool_transform.cc
+++ b/plugins/tools/tool_transform2/kis_tool_transform.cc
@@ -903,6 +903,19 @@ void KisToolTransform::novaRotate90(bool clockwise)
     QMetaObject::invokeMethod(m_optionsWidget, clockwise ? "slotRotateCW" : "slotRotateCCW");
 }
 
+void KisToolTransform::novaSetTransformMode(KisToolTransform::TransformToolMode newMode)
+{
+    if (m_optionsWidget) {
+        setTransformMode(newMode); // through the options widget, which follows
+        return;
+    }
+    const ToolTransformArgs::TransformMode mode = toArgsMode(newMode);
+    if (mode != m_currentArgs.mode()) {
+        slotResetTransform(mode);
+        Q_EMIT transformModeChanged();
+    }
+}
+
